 5 · Reading the print 







body{margin:0}


 5 · Reading the print The person is the sensor: a photo of the tower, with the numbers readable, sent as the app sends a photo, the picture above the words. The agent names the block and why, then proposes one write. Nothing here is a temperature widget: the proposal is a Chat/Tool Activity card whose rows are the ordinary settings preview (the setting, old → new, and the preset it is saved as), filled from the test’s declaration. The outcome of every test is the same thing, a new preset; nothing is written until “Save preset”. Temperature tower for Gray PETG Setup summary Current Temperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4 0.20mm Standard · Gray PETG 240 → 210 °C in 5 °C blocks; read the cleanest block 48 min 11 g All settings Here it is. Worked for 12s · 1 action 225 °C is the cleanest block: no hairs between the posts and the bridges are straight. 230 °C shows fine hairs; 220 °C and below look dull and the layers bond less well. I would set Gray PETG to 225 °C on this printer. Save 225 °C as a new filament preset New preset · Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated Nozzle temperature 240 → 225 °C Gray PETG itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another block Ask about this print or request a change… Claude Opus 5.5 Thinking: Medium Send 


